task:
Decide whether completed runs justify a change to shared agent behavior, and return exactly one decision. First perform the same bounded evidence pass as the reviewer: (1) (runs/list-runs 20 nil), without return; (2) choose a run and call (runs/review-seed run-id), which returns its filtered errors, final exact generated program, and final exact model response through three audited source reads in one evaluation. The compact seed omits the cumulative model-request transcript; call runs/latest-model-exchange only if that transcript is necessary to justify the decision. Do not open unfiltered turn pages or traverse older private pages during this initial pass. (runs/provenance run-id) identifies component replacements. (runs/effective-prelude run-id component-id) returns the source actually executed by that run; repository tools return the current workspace source. Compare their identities when historical behavior depends on a component. If those records show a reusable behavior gap, use repo/search, repo/find-files, or repo/read-range to read only the component that owns it before proposing a change. Otherwise decide without spending the remaining turns on speculative browsing. Treat every runs/* or repo/* result as an intermediate observation and never return it directly; use return only for the final decision. Return one map matching exactly one of these shapes, with PTC-Lisp string keys and never a bare decision string. A trailing ? marks an optional key; every other key is required.
{"candidate" {"base_source_hash" string, "component_id" string, "content" string, "format" "component-source"}, "decision" "propose-change", "evaluation_plan" {"metrics" [string], "motivating_cases" [string], "regression_cases" [string], "held_out_cases"? [string]}, "evidence" [{"positions" [integer], "provider" string, "resource" string, "snapshot_hash" string}], "generalized_failure" string, "target" string, "review_diff"? string, "risks"? [string]}
{"decision" "no-change", "evidence" [{"positions" [integer], "provider" string, "resource" string, "snapshot_hash" string}], "rationale" string}
{"decision" "insufficient-evidence", "missing_evidence" [string], "rationale" string}
Choose "propose-change" only when the evidence shows a reusable gap that would recur on inputs unlike the ones examined, and its generalized_failure must hold independently of any single run. Choose "no-change" when sufficient evidence shows only an isolated defect. Choose "insufficient-evidence" when the captured providers cannot settle the question, and say what must be captured. Copy candidate.base_source_hash exactly from the matching item's sha256-prefixed source_hash returned by runs/effective-prelude. Return complete replacement source, not a diff. Do not invent a candidate source hash: trusted host materialization computes SHA-256 from the exact returned content. Copy every evidence provider and snapshot_hash exactly from the runs/* or repo/* response that produced it. For history or private-history, resource is the run ID and positions are event sequence IDs. For workspace, resource is the relative path and positions are the source line numbers cited. Do not cite a response that lacks provider or snapshot_hash. Keep reasoning out of evidence. A single failing run is not by itself a reusable gap, and an unsupported proposal fails evaluation even when its patch looks reasonable.
